# Easy API ↔ Firestore Integration Guide

This doc captures the current Firestore-backed data model and the conventions for layering the Easy API on top of (or eventually replacing) it. It's the working brief for any session that touches Easy API integration — keep it up to date as endpoints are wired in.

> Code entry point: [lib/easy-api/server.ts](lib/easy-api/server.ts) — `EasyApiService` class + `easyApi` singleton.
> Auth: `x-easy-api-key` header sourced from `process.env.API_SECRET_KEY`. Base URL from `process.env.API_BASE_URL` (no `/v1` suffix — paths in domain modules must include their own version segment if needed).

---

## 0. Product context

Beni Capital is an investment platform where users back **projects** (theatre / film / TV / music — see [types/project.d.ts](types/project.d.ts)) and later receive returns. The end goal of the Easy API integration is to **enable real-money investment payments** — Easy API is the chosen payment provider in place of Stripe.

That means most Easy API endpoints will be in service of the **invest → pay → confirm → record** flow:

1. User picks a project on the dashboard (existing UI).
2. App initiates a payment via Easy API (new — `lib/easy-api/payments.ts` or similar when endpoints arrive).
3. Easy API returns a payment intent / checkout URL / status — shape TBD.
4. On success, a `Transaction` (`type: 'investment'`) is recorded — currently in Firestore via [lib/firebase/transaction-actions.ts](lib/firebase/transaction-actions.ts), eventually mirrored or replaced through Easy API.
5. Project's `moneyRaised` is updated; user dashboard reflects the new investment.

### When a new endpoint arrives, expect to touch:

| Layer | What may change | Files to check |
|---|---|---|
| **Easy API domain module** | New methods on `easyApi` for the endpoint. | [lib/easy-api/](lib/easy-api/) |
| **Project type** | Payment-related fields on `Project` (e.g. payment account ID, payout config, fee structure). | [types/project.d.ts](types/project.d.ts), `Financials`, `InvestmentTerms` |
| **Transaction type** | New fields linking to Easy API entities (payment ID, status, settlement date, fee). | [types/transaction.ts](types/transaction.ts) |
| **Firestore rules / actions** | New collections (e.g. `payments`, `payouts`); new fields under existing docs; rule updates for who can read payment metadata. | [firestore.rules](firestore.rules), [lib/firebase/](lib/firebase/) |
| **Dashboard UI** | Surfacing payment status, receipts, retry/cancel flows, payout tracking. | [app/(dashboard)/](app/(dashboard)/), [modules/dashboard/](modules/dashboard/) |
| **API routes** | New `app/api/*` routes that call Easy API on behalf of the user (after Firebase ID-token check). | [app/api/](app/api/) |

When the user provides an endpoint, **don't just wire the HTTP call** — walk this table and ask which layers need to move.

