### Required type changes
- [types/project.d.ts](types/project.d.ts) — **no Easy API fields**. Tiers are global. `Financials.minInvestment` becomes display-only (the real minimum is the lowest tier).
- [types/transaction.ts](types/transaction.ts) —
  ```ts
  status: 'pending' | 'succeeded' | 'failed' | 'expired' | 'canceled';
  amountCents: number;
  currency: 'USD';
  tierDollars: 5000 | 10000 | 25000 | 50000 | 100000 | 250000;
  easyApiPaymentLinkId: string;
  easyApiPaymentId?: string;
  ```
  Pre-launch — convert callers in one pass; don't dual-write `amount`/`amountCents`.
- [firestore.rules](firestore.rules) — `status`, `easyApiPaymentLinkId`, `easyApiPaymentId`, `amountCents` must be **server-only writes**. Users may not flip their own transaction to `succeeded`.

### Required new code
- `scripts/setup-easy-api-products.ts` — one-time bootstrap. Creates the Product + 6 Prices via `/v1/api/products/` and `/v1/api/product-prices/`. Prints the 7 IDs. Run once per environment, paste into `.env.local`. Use `metadata.bootstrap_id: 'beni-investment-v1'` so re-runs are detectable.
- `lib/easy-api/products.ts` — typed `createProduct`, `createProductPrice`. Used only by the bootstrap script.
- `lib/easy-api/payments.ts` — `createPaymentLink({ project, user, tierDollars, transactionId })`. Resolves tier → priceId from env; builds the body; calls Easy API.
- `app/api/easy-api/payment-link/route.ts` — verifies Firebase ID token, loads project, validates project status `=== 'fundraising'`, creates a `pending` Transaction in Firestore (server-only fields), then calls `createPaymentLink`, returns `{ url }`. Idempotency workaround: dedupe a pending Transaction for `(userId, projectId, tierDollars)` < 5 min old; reuse the URL.
- `app/api/easy-api/webhook/route.ts` — **source of truth for payment success**. Verifies signature with `EASY_API_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, switches on event type, reads `tags.transactionId`, idempotently updates Transaction + `Project.moneyRaised`.
- `app/payment/success/page.tsx`, `app/payment/canceled/page.tsx` — UX only. Don't trust the URL for state; show "confirming…" and let the webhook drive the data (poll the Transaction by `?t=<id>` or use a Firestore listener).
- Dashboard: 6 tier buttons on project pages; modules under [app/(dashboard)/](app/(dashboard)/) and [modules/dashboard/](modules/dashboard/).

### Webhook events to subscribe to
Configure in the Easy API dashboard (per the screenshot UI). Endpoint URL: `https://benicapital.com/api/easy-api/webhook`. Must be HTTPS. Subscribe to **only what we handle**:

| Event | Action |
|---|---|
| `payment.created` | Optional log. Pending Transaction already exists. |
| `payment.updated` | **Primary.** Map status → `succeeded`/`failed`/`canceled`/`expired`; on success, increment `Project.moneyRaised` (Firestore transaction). |
| `refund.created`, `refund.updated` | Mark Transaction refunded; decrement `moneyRaised`. |
| `dispute.created`, `dispute.updated` | Flag for admin review; **do not** auto-decrement `moneyRaised` — admin decides. |

Skip `authorization.*` (covered by `payment.updated`), `subscription.*` (we're one-time only), `identity.*` (Firebase Auth owns user identity).

### Order of implementation
1. Pin the open questions in §10 (especially webhook signature scheme).
2. Bootstrap script → run once → copy 7 IDs into `.env.local`.
3. Tier constants + env reader util.
4. Type changes + Firestore rule tightening.
5. Domain modules + create-link route.
6. Webhook route.
7. Dashboard tier buttons + return pages.

